  "comments": {
    "comments": {},
    "bugs": {
      "18583": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": 3216,
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 100056,
            "time": "2023-08-25T15:14:28Z",
            "creation_time": "2023-08-25T15:14:28Z",
            "creator": "jaganmn2",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 0,
            "bug_id": 18583,
            "text": "Created attachment 3216\npatch for cbind.ts(deparse.level=)\n\nNote that a fix for this bug is more or less conditional on a fix for Bug 18579, as `cbind.ts` is currently only ever dispatched with `deparse.level = 1`.  But even then, we see:\n\n```\n> body(stats:::cbind.ts)\n{\n    if (deparse.level != 1) \n        .NotYetUsed(\"deparse.level != 1\")\n    .cbind.ts(list(...), .makeNamesTs(...), dframe = FALSE, union = TRUE)\n}\n```\n\n`cbind.ts` does not really behave as the internal default method does when `deparse.level = 1`.  Untagged arguments are named by `.makeNamesTs` as if `deparse.level = 2`.  That is, they are deparsed unconditionally:\n\n```\n> body(stats:::.makeNamesTs)\n{\n    l <- as.list(substitute(list(...)))[-1L]\n    nm <- names(l)\n    fixup <- if (is.null(nm)) \n        seq_along(l)\n    else nm == \"\"\n    dep <- sapply(l[fixup], function(x) deparse(x)[1L])\n    if (is.null(nm)) \n        return(dep)\n    if (any(fixup)) \n        nm[fixup] <- dep\n    nm\n}\n```\n\nA corollary is that the return value of `cbind.ts` always has non-`NULL` column names.  Another difference is that matrices with 2 or more columns have their column names formatted in the result as `paste(<name>, colnames(.), sep=\".\")` or `paste(<name>, seq_len(ncol(.)), sep=\".\")`.\n\nObviously, for backwards compatibility, this behaviour should be more or less preserved when `missing(deparse.level)` is `TRUE`.  Hence I propose the following changes:\n\n1. In the `missing(deparse.level)=FALSE` case, the column names of the `cbind.ts` result should be determined exactly as they are determined the internal default method.\n2. In the `missing(deparse.level)= TRUE` case, _all_ matrices (i.e., not only those with two or more columns) should have their column names formatted with `paste(..., sep=\".\")`.\n\nThe attached patch implements these changes more or less by:\n\n* Refactoring the helper `.makeNamesTs` to behave according to a `deparse.level` argument.\n* Refactoring the helper `.cbind.ts` to behave according to a `doDot` argument, i.e., \"as before\" (modulo Change 2) when `doDot=TRUE` and as the internal default method for `cbind` when `doDot=FALSE`.\n* Adjusting methods `cbind.ts` and `Ops.ts` and exported functions `ts.union` and `ts.intersect`, which each call `.makeNamesTs` and/or `.cbind.ts`.\n* Adjusting method `summary.stl` which is affected by Change 2.\n\nI suppose that a more conservative patch would omit Change 2, and I can provide one if that path is preferred.  One need only omit the changes to `summary.stl` and adjust some logic in `.cbind.ts` ..."
          },
          {
            "count": 1,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "text": "I should add that this \"bug\" is perhaps really a feature request, given that:\n\n* `cbind.ts` is aliased in `help(\"ts\")` but nowhere documented\n* `cbind.data.frame` does not use `deparse.level` and is documented accordingly in help(\"cbind\") (\"just a wrapper for `data.frame(..., check.names = FALSE)`\")\n* `help(\"cbind\")` hints that `deparse.level` need not be used by methods other than the internal default method (\"integer controlling the construction of labels in the case of non-matrix-like arguments (for the default method)\")\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n* users would be right to expect classes `mts` and `ts` to be handled as traditional matrices and vectors by the method for `cbind` (modulo alignment of `tsp[1:2]`)\n* `methods:::cbind` handles most cases of `base::cbind(..., <S4>, ...)` and _does_ respect `deparse.level`",
            "bug_id": 18583,
            "creator": "jaganmn2",
            "creation_time": "2023-08-25T17:40:00Z",
            "is_private": false,
            "time": "2023-08-25T17:40:00Z",
            "id": 100057,
            "attachment_id": {},
