            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": {},
            "text": "I agree that this is a reasonable WISHLIST / feature request.\n\nOTOH, my gut feeling was that the patch is relatively extensive, adding quite a bit more code (to be maintained, etc) than I'd had assumed intuitively...\nHence confirmed (but of minor importance ..).\n\n{OTOH, Bug 18579 really *was* unfortunate and the solution we ended with there,\n using new `R_missing()` was really nice}.",
            "bug_id": 18583,
            "count": 2,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creator": "maechler",
            "creation_time": "2023-10-20T19:21:41Z"
          },
          {
            "count": 3,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "text": "Created attachment 3307\nditto with smaller diff\n\nReturning with less tired eyes, I was able to shrink the diff (63->47 lines added, 31->23 lines removed).  I would say that the apparent complexity of the remaining changes reflects the _actual_ complexity of the way that the internal `cbind` constructs `dimnames` as a function of `deparse.level`.\n\nThis patch replaces one instance of `if(is.null(A)) B else A` (in the code written by me) with `A %||% B`.",
